    {
      "filename": "Dover Castle (EH) 20-04-2012 (7217044814).jpg",
      "title": "File:Dover Castle (EH) 20-04-2012 (7217044814).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/49/Dover_Castle_%28EH%29_20-04-2012_%287217044814%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dover_Castle_(EH)_20-04-2012_(7217044814).jpg",
      "width": 2047,
      "height": 1347,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Karen Roe from Bury St Edmunds, Suffolk, UK, United Kingdom",
      "credit": "Dover Castle (EH) 20-04-2012",
      "source": "Dover Castle (EH) 20-04-2012 (7217044814)",
      "description": "For a great family day out in Kent visit Dover Castle, open all year round. Immerse yourself in our dramatic new visitor experience, Operation Dynamo: Rescue from Dunkirk, open now to visitors. \nSpectacularly situated above the White Cliffs of Dover this magnificent castle has guarded our shores from invasion for 20 centuries - now you can enjoy a great family day out with a visit to the 'Key to England'.\nExplore the darkly atmospheric Secret Wartime Tunnels now with a vivid recreation of the Dunkirk evacuation, complete with dramatic projections of swooping Spitfires and real film footage. Watch Heart FM's breakfast team James &amp; Charlie as they experience Operation Dynamo. \nEnjoy a colourful contrast with the richly-furnished Great Tower, where costumed actors introduce medieval life at King Henry II's court.\n\nWith exciting exhibitions, winding tunnels to explore, ghosts to hunt out - and of course restaurants, shops and the space for youngsters to run around - an action-packed, great value day out awaits!",
      "dateCreated": "2012-04-20 12:26",
      "sourceType": "core",
      "sourceArticleId": "white-cliffs-of-dover-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "u10f"
    },
